# One newline convention in every checkout.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout hands every text file back with CRLF. A test
# that reads a file and matches a pattern written against "\n" then finds nothing
# and reports the file as malformed - green on Linux and macOS, red on the Windows
# matrix, about a file nobody touched. That happened once; this is the fix for the
# class rather than for the one test.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A patch carries its own line endings. Rewriting them makes it fail to apply.
*.patch -text
